    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-head",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4414,
      "width": 600,
      "height": 33.599999999999994,
      "text": "Decided so far",
      "fontSize": 24,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4458,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 44.8,
      "text": "✓ What deadline data can evams hand to RPM?: a public JSON feed with stable IDs and IST deadlines, ~6 h fresh;\nRPM can pull it with no evams change.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4522,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 44.8,
      "text": "✓ How do Google Calendar and Google Tasks sync both ways with Convex?: Calendar pushes changes, Tasks must be\npolled; Tasks keeps dates but not times; OAuth must be production-unverified.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4586,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 44.8,
      "text": "✓ Can an agent loop run on the small VM, fast enough?: yes; Pi + Claude Haiku finished 3 of 3 runs at ~120 MB\npeak, 11–16 s per 5-step task, nearly all model time. grokbot was checked and rejected.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4650,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 22.4,
      "text": "✓ Get Oracle's free Ampere A1 VM: not needed; the small VM is enough for now.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4690,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 67.19999999999999,
      "text": "✓ What exactly are Routines, water reminders and the meal log?: Routines run in fixed windows with tick-off\nsteps; water every 90 min with one-tap glasses; meals logged in one tap from recent favourites; agent\nestimates kept apart as guesses.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4778,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 44.8,
      "text": "✓ How does Pi on the VM talk over Telegram and call RPM tools?: a small Node bridge long-polls Telegram and\ndrives Pi in RPC mode; RPM tools come in as a Pi extension; ~180 MB.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4842,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 44.8,
      "text": "✓ Read and compare the evams deadline feed: built on a branch; 30 tests pass; live feed has 41 assessments, 11\nwithout a clock time.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-decided-7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4906,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 44.8,
      "text": "✓ Build the Telegram bridge for Pi: built on a branch, 24 tests pass; waits for your bot token and chat ID to\ngo live.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "strokeColor": "#1e2a3a",
      "fontFamily": "helvetica"
    },
    {
      "id": "rpm-oos-head",
      "type": "text",
